course: dictionary
lesson: 9107
title: A word from modern life
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A smartphone is a mobile phone that is also a small computer. «She checked the news on her smartphone before school.» The clues are phone and computer: you can make calls, but you can also go online and use apps. Smart means clever, so a smartphone is a clever phone.
explain: Smartphone is a noun, so you can have one smartphone or several smartphones. It is a compound word, made from two smaller words, smart and phone. Ask yourself what each part means, then put them together.
explain: Some sentences tell you when something began. «The first mobile phones in the 1980s were as big as bricks, and from 2007 smartphones with touch screens began to spread.» The dates show that smartphones are newer than the big phones of the 1980s.
fact: A smartphone is a mobile phone that is also a small computer.
fact: A smartphone can go online, take photos, play games, use apps and make calls.
fact: «Smartphones became common after 2007», so they are a modern invention.
fact: «Smartphones are assembled from parts made by many companies», and many of the factories are in China, India and Vietnam.
fact: An anachronism is something that belongs to another time, such as a Viking with a smartphone.
exercise: «She checked the news on her smartphone before school.» What is a smartphone? | A kind of bicycle | A large clock that hangs on a wall | A book with pictures in it | *A mobile phone that is also a small computer
exercise: «From 2007 smartphones with touch screens began to spread.» Which year did smartphones start to spread? | 2005 | 1980 | *2007 | 1991
exercise: Which one does NOT belong to its time? | A knight in armour | A farmer with a plough | A Roman soldier with a sword | *A Roman soldier with a wristwatch
test:
«Smartphones are assembled from parts made by many companies.» What does assembled mean? | *Put together from parts | Thrown away | Painted a bright colour | Sold in a shop
Which is NOT something a smartphone can do? | Make calls | Take photos | *Grow plants in a garden | Use apps
exam:
According to the lesson, what is a smartphone? | A camera and a clock | A book and a radio | *A mobile phone and a small computer | A car and a bike
